  objectName: Eclipse
  thumbnail: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 48f8186603548496f8d631d617efee42, type: 3}
  detailImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 48f8186603548496f8d631d617efee42, type: 3}
  description: An eclipse occurs when one celestial object blocks light from another
    or moves into its shadow. A solar eclipse happens when the Moon passes between
    Earth and the Sun, while a lunar eclipse occurs when Earth blocks sunlight from
    reaching the Moon.
  interestingFact: During a total solar eclipse, the Moon completely covers the Sun
    as seen from a narrow region of Earth's surface, revealing the Sun's outer atmosphere,
    called the corona.
  objectType: 8
